1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,112
Narrator: Scenario 1. Global meeting communication.

2
00:00:05,712 --> 00:00:18,672
A: I support production operations for the APAC region. My responsibilities include infrastructure checks, application monitoring, deployment support, and incident coordination.

3
00:00:19,272 --> 00:00:28,656
B: Thanks for the introduction. When an application problem requires a code change, does your team make that change or involve another owner?

4
00:00:29,256 --> 00:00:39,984
A: The application team owns code changes. We gather operational evidence, coordinate the response, and help validate the service after their fix is deployed.

5
00:00:40,584 --> 00:00:49,608
B: That helps. How should the global team contact you during your coverage hours, and who takes over after your regional shift ends?

6
00:00:50,208 --> 00:01:00,096
A: Please use the shared operations channel during our shift. For urgent incidents, page the current on-call engineer through the incident system.

7
00:01:00,696 --> 00:01:10,464
B: Could you clarify whether your team also approves production changes? Some regional requests have been sent directly to individual engineers.

8
00:01:11,064 --> 00:01:22,200
A: We review operational readiness, but the designated change approver authorizes production changes. Sending a request to us does not replace that approval.

9
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:34,200
B: Understood. Please join our weekly service review and highlight regional risks, especially capacity concerns or repeated incidents that need broader support.

10
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:43,440
A: I can do that. Would you prefer a short written update beforehand so the meeting can focus on decisions and blocked items?

11
00:01:44,040 --> 00:01:54,024
B: Yes. Post the update one business day before the review, with the impact, current owner, and any decision needed from this group.

12
00:01:54,624 --> 00:02:04,392
A: I will share our coverage schedule and responsibility map by 16:00 UTC tomorrow, including the handoff process and escalation contacts.

13
00:02:04,992 --> 00:02:14,664
B: Great. I will review those details and add you to the recurring meeting. We can resolve any remaining ownership gaps there.
